    "notes": "1. Total revenue is constructed as the sum of all revenue line items from the statement, including Interest income. The primary statement shows 'Total net revenue' as the sum of Noninterest revenue and Net interest income; this mapping decomposes it into its components. 2. Total operating cost includes all expenses that are part of operations before income tax: Interest expense, Provision for credit losses, and all Noninterest expense components (Compensation, Occupancy, Technology, Professional, Marketing, Other). This follows standard banking industry practice where interest expense and credit loss provisions are key operating costs. 3. Taxes and interest expenses are taken directly from the statement. The sign convention is followed: these are positive numbers as they reduce income. 4. Investment securities losses and other negative revenue components are included as negative numbers in total_revenue. 5. All values are in millions (scale 1E6) as indicated in the statement.",
